er the years, he rose through the ranks, becoming a leading figure in the institution's research community."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 588, "end": 728, "text": "\"Dietmar was an exceptional researcher and an invaluable asset to our faculty,\" said Professor Rachel Levy, Dean of the Faculty of Medicine."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 729, "end": 909, "text": "\"His dedication to advancing medical knowledge and improving human health was inspiring, and his work continues to have a profound impact on our understanding of various diseases.\""}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 910, "end": 1060, "text": "During his tenure, Krautwurst published numerous papers in top-tier scientific journals, including the prestigious _Nature Medicine_ and _The Lancet_."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1061, "end": 1181, "text": "His research focused on the molecular mechanisms underlying cancer, neurodegenerative diseases, and infectious diseases."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1182, "end": 1307, "text": "One of Krautwurst's most notable achievements was his discovery of a novel therapeutic target for treating pancreatic cancer."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1308, "end": 1420, "text": "His findings, published in a 2015 paper, have since led to the development of several promising drug candidates."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1421, "end": 1482, "text": "\"Working with Dietmar was an incredible experience,\" said Dr."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1483, "end": 1540, "text": "Maya Cohen, a former research fellow in Krautwurst's lab."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1541, "end": 1585, "text": "\"He was a mentor, a colleague, and a friend."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1586, "end": 1722, "text": "His passion for science was contagious, and he instilled in us a sense of curiosity and creativity that has stayed with me to this day.\""}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1723, "end": 1804, "text": "Krautwurst's contributions to the Faculty of Medicine extend beyond his research."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1805, "end": 1901, "text": "He was an esteemed teacher, supervising numerous graduate students and postdoctoral researchers."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1902, "end": 2011, "text": "He also served on several departmental committees, helping to shape the faculty's research agenda and policy."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2012, "end": 2137, "text": "According to data from the Faculty of Medicine, Krautwurst's research has been cited over 5,000 times, with an h-index of 42."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2138, "end": 2298, "text": "His work has attracted significant funding from national and international agencies, including the Israeli Ministry of Health and the European Research Council."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2299, "end": 2467, "text": "While Krautwurst's departure from the Faculty of Medicine marks the end of an era, his legacy will continue to inspire and influence the next generation of researchers."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Dietmar Krautwurst", "scope": "organization", "claim": "Dietmar Krautwurst worked for the Leibniz-Institute for Food Systems Biology at the Technical University of Munich.", "answer": "Leibniz-Institute for Food Systems Biology at the Technical University of Munich", "quote": "Krautwurst has worked at the Leibniz-Institute for Food Systems Biology at the Technical University of Munich, a facility located in Freising, Germany.", "original_document_number": 1}], "current_answers": ["Leibniz-Institute for Food Systems Biology at the